  "notes": "Compton’s guitar-first bedroom auteur — an alt-R&B/funk lane inside West Coast rap. Three parameters carry it and all three are sourced. **The guitar is the lead voice and the harmony source**, written on guitar so the voicings are guitar-shaped: root-omitted, 3rd-and-7th stacks, maj7/m9/add9 with chromatic passing chords. **The bass is played electric, not an 808** — syncopated and melodic across E1–C3, no glides. And the record is tracked into an iPhone through an iRig, which **caps the layer count** and gives the lo-fi, slightly-clipped timbre; the drums are the least-processed element. ⚠ `medium`: method and lineage are high-confidence, the tempo band is marked `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
